  "id": "COMPOUND:20924 - PROTEIN:6326",
  "verbalization": "Uralsaponin Y is implicated in the target pathway leading to Phosphodiesterase 6C through multiple indirect routes. The evidence suggests that Uralsaponin Y acts as a target for K562, which in turn is a target of two distinct compounds—1-(1-Methylpyrrolidin-2-yl)propan-2-ol and Hirsutalin H. Both of these compounds are ultimately linked to Phosphodiesterase 6C, indicating a potential shared mechanism of action or a hierarchical pathway in which Uralsaponin Y may influence the activity of these intermediates. The presence of multiple pathways converging on Phosphodiesterase 6C suggests that Uralsaponin Y may exert its effects through a series of molecular interactions that ultimately modulate the activity of this enzyme. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the target network and underscores the importance of understanding the interplay between these compounds in the context of their biological roles.",
